diff -ruN v012_documents_base/PLANNING_DOCUMENT_ACQUISITION.md v012_documents_work/PLANNING_DOCUMENT_ACQUISITION.md
--- v012_documents_base/PLANNING_DOCUMENT_ACQUISITION.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ v012_documents_work/PLANNING_DOCUMENT_ACQUISITION.md	2026-08-05 18:36:02.613887495 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Planning document acquisition
+
+ThemePark Map can automatically catalogue geometry-relevant documents linked from bounded Planning Data application records.
+
+## Safety model
+
+The acquisition engine follows only:
+
+1. direct `document-urls` supplied by the planning record;
+2. the record's `documentation-url` or `application-url`;
+3. one same-host page explicitly labelled Documents, Plans, Drawings, Attachments, or Files.
+
+It does not perform unrestricted web crawling, authenticate to portals, bypass access controls, submit comments, or scrape search results unrelated to the bounded Planning Data records.
+
+## Modes
+
+- `off`: do not inspect planning documents.
+- `discover`: catalogue candidate links without downloading files.
+- `download`: cache selected geometry-relevant PDFs and images.
+- `extract`: download selected files and inspect embedded PDF text with `pdftotext` when available.
+
+Downloaded documents remain in the response cache. They are not copied into the generated `.mcworld` or build artifact because public visibility does not imply a redistribution licence.
+
+## Candidate ranking
+
+High-value drawing classes include:
+
+- site, block and master plans;
+- landscape and planting plans;
+- ride or track layouts;
+- floor, roof, elevation and section drawings;
+- drainage, level, topographic, access and lighting plans.
+
+Application forms, comments, representations, correspondence, fee documents, privacy material and superseded drawings are rejected by default.
+
+## Authority boundary
+
+A downloaded or classified plan is evidence only. It cannot replace OpenStreetMap geometry. A later vector/georeferencing stage must produce provenance-complete GeoJSON, and that geometry must still pass the Phase 18 planning-authority status, confidence, overlap, offset and ambiguity gates.
+
+## CLI example
+
+```bash
+node src/cli.mjs build \
+  --planning-data \
+  --planning-documents \
+  --planning-document-mode extract \
+  --planning-document-max-applications 80 \
+  --planning-document-max-documents 240 \
+  --planning-document-max-mb 25 \
+  --planning-document-max-pages 5
+```
+
+The output includes `planning-document-catalogue.json` with the application reference, source pages, discovered candidates, classification, selection decision, download hash, byte size, cache status, embedded-text hash and reuse status.
